From: local backport
Subject: usb: gadget: f_ncm: retry a timer flush when USB TX is busy

Based on Cosmin Tanislav's linux-usb patch, 2026-08-17:
https://lore.kernel.org/linux-usb/20260817192638.437798-1-cosmin-gabriel.tanislav.xa@renesas.com/

A timer-originated flush has no qdisc to requeue NETDEV_TX_BUSY. Keep the
existing 300us deadline and retry instead of leaving the NTB stranded.
Advance the expiration before HRTIMER_RESTART to avoid an expired-timer
busy loop. Existing small-frame flushing, aggregation and USB PM stay intact.

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
@@ -1158,7 +1158,11 @@
 		 *
 		 * This will call directly into u_ether's eth_start_xmit()
 		 */
-		netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev);
+		/* A timer flush has no qdisc to retry a busy USB request. */
+		if (netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev) == NETDEV_TX_BUSY) {
+			hrtimer_forward_now(data, TX_TIMEOUT_NSECS);
+			return HRTIMER_RESTART;
+		}
 	}
 	return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 }
